From: Lewis Gibson <12851394+lewisgibson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:21:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not report halted regions in the watchdog

When the server stops, the region scheduler halts its threads while a
tick that was running on one of them can still be registered with the
watchdog. The watchdog then reports "Tick region ... has not responded"
for a region that is shutting down, and ThreadMXBean#getThreadInfo
returns null for a thread that has already exited, so
WatchdogThread#dumpThread throws a NullPointerException and the Folia
Watchdog Thread dies with an uncaught exception.

Skip a tick whose thread is no longer alive, and skip the dump if the
thread exits between that check and the dump.

diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/FoliaWatchdogThread.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/FoliaWatchdogThread.java
index e9ca1a15049b0211d10401cb78e953b93afaf6c7..4b610ab67b8d7fbce7dca26a612ea9cbc5eebd4b 100644
--- a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/FoliaWatchdogThread.java
+++ b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/FoliaWatchdogThread.java
@@ -68,6 +68,9 @@ public final class FoliaWatchdogThread extends Thread {
                 if (elapsed <= TimeUnit.SECONDS.toNanos(5L)) {
                     continue;
                 }
+                if (!tick.thread.isAlive()) { // Folia - watchdog - the scheduler halted this thread while the tick was still registered
+                    continue;
+                }
                 tick.lastPrint = now;
 
                 final double totalElapsedS = (double)(now - tick.start) / 1.0E9;
@@ -82,10 +85,11 @@ public final class FoliaWatchdogThread extends Thread {
                     LOGGER.error("Global region has not responded in " + totalElapsedS + "s:");
                 }
 
-                WatchdogThread.dumpThread(
-                    ManagementFactory.getThreadMXBean().getThreadInfo(tick.thread.threadId(), Integer.MAX_VALUE),
-                    Bukkit.getServer().getLogger()
-                );
+                final java.lang.management.ThreadInfo threadInfo = ManagementFactory.getThreadMXBean().getThreadInfo(tick.thread.threadId(), Integer.MAX_VALUE); // Folia - watchdog
+                if (threadInfo == null) { // Folia - watchdog - the thread exited after the check above
+                    continue;
+                }
+                WatchdogThread.dumpThread(threadInfo, Bukkit.getServer().getLogger());
             }
         }
     }
